RING3EXEC (rmbp-ledger B521) — user-midden's half, as a patch against MIDDENTWIN's program
(exec-rmbp-middentwin @07c514e7, unaos/crates/user-midden/src/main.rs). The crate is not on RING3EXEC's base;
the seat applies this at the fold, after MIDDENTWIN lands:  git apply docs/dev/evidence/ring3exec/user-midden.patch
What it does: Facts::ring3 with exec ON (x86: the kernel carries SYS_SPAWN_PATH); `run <path> [args]` served
through midden_core::resolve_exec + SYS_SPAWN_PATH; bare names (Plan::Exec) launched the same way; the wire line
`:: MIDDEN: plan=Exec verb=<run|typed> served=1 pid=<n> ::` (or `served=0 err=<errno>`); `ls <dir>` unchanged in
code (SYS_PATH_READ + PATH_R_LIST), now governed kernel-side by the ownership ACL; errno texts updated.
